# Git merge: never fast-forward

Never fast-forward. Not as a default, not when history is linear, not to "keep it simple."

When merging (including "merge into \<branch\>"):

- Always `git merge --no-ff`
- Never `git merge --ff`, `--ff-only`, or a merge that fast-forwards because `merge.ff` is unset/true
- Never `git pull --ff-only` to achieve a fast-forward onto the target branch

A merge the user asked for is a **merge commit** with two parents. Completing a commit on a feature branch is not permission to fast-forward the integration branch.
